DSPy’s wrapper logic lives in `Module.__call__` and `acall`, not in a direct `forward(...)` call. That wrapper is also where usage-tracking attachment happens, and it only knows how to attach usage when the module returns a `dspy.Prediction` or a tuple whose first element is a `Prediction`. Returning some other shape still works functionally, but it cannot carry that bookkeeping. Program:
import dspy
from dspy.utils.dummies import DummyLM
class Good(dspy.Module):
    def __init__(self): super().__init__(); self.p = dspy.Predict('q -> a')
    def forward(self, q): return self.p(q=q)
class TupleGood(dspy.Module):
    def __init__(self): super().__init__(); self.p = dspy.Predict('q -> a')
    def forward(self, q): return self.p(q=q), {'meta': 1}
class Bad(dspy.Module):
    def __init__(self): super().__init__(); self.p = dspy.Predict('q -> a')
    def forward(self, q): return {'a': self.p(q=q).a}
dspy.configure(lm=DummyLM([{'a': 'x'}, {'a': 'y'}, {'a': 'z'}, {'a': 'w'}]))
print(type(Good()(q='1')).__name__)
print(type(TupleGood()(q='2')[0]).__name__)
print(Bad()(q='3'))
print(Good().forward(q='4'))

DSPy only routes an annotation through the native-type path when it is actually a class of the expected kind. In `Adapter._call_preprocess` the check is `isinstance(annotation, type)` before `issubclass`, and in adapter utilities it uses `inspect.isclass(...)` before `issubclass`. That is why generic aliases such as the `next_tool_args` annotation in ReAct do not crash the runtime. Program:
import dspy, dspy.adapters.base as adapter_base, dspy.adapters.utils as adapter_utils
from dspy.utils.dummies import DummyLM
def get_user_info(name: str): return {'name': name}
class Sig(dspy.Signature):
    user_request: str = dspy.InputField()
    process_result: str = dspy.OutputField()
react = dspy.ReAct(Sig, tools=[get_user_info])
problem = react.react.signature.output_fields['next_tool_args'].annotation
def guarded(cls, base):
    if cls == problem: raise TypeError('issubclass() arg 1 must be a class')
    return issubclass(cls, base)
adapter_base.issubclass = guarded
adapter_utils.issubclass = guarded
dspy.configure(lm=DummyLM([{'next_thought': 'look up user', 'next_tool_name': 'get_user_info', 'next_tool_args': {'name': 'Adam'}}, {'next_thought': 'done', 'next_tool_name': 'finish', 'next_tool_args': {}}, {'reasoning': 'used tool output', 'process_result': 'Resolved Adam'}]))
print(react(user_request='Help me, my name is Adam').process_result)
